>>SOURCE FORMAT FREE
*> Circular primes below 100 (rotation of one- and two-digit numbers); expect 13.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CIRCULAR-PRIMES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-COUNT   PIC 9(9) VALUE 0.
01 WS-P       PIC 9(9).
01 WS-N       PIC 9(9).
01 WS-D       PIC 9(9).
01 WS-Q       PIC 9(9).
01 WS-R       PIC 9(9).
01 WS-PRIME   PIC 9 VALUE 0.
01 WS-ROT PIC 9(9).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    PERFORM VARYING WS-P FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-P >= 100
        MOVE WS-P TO WS-N
        PERFORM CHECK-PRIME
        IF WS-PRIME = 1
            IF WS-P < 10
                ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
            ELSE
                DIVIDE WS-P BY 10 GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER WS-R
                COMPUTE WS-N = WS-R * 10 + WS-Q
                PERFORM CHECK-PRIME
                IF WS-PRIME = 1 ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT END-IF
            END-IF
        END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY WS-COUNT
    STOP RUN.
CHECK-PRIME.
    MOVE 1 TO WS-PRIME
    IF WS-N < 2 MOVE 0 TO WS-PRIME END-IF
    PERFORM VARYING WS-D FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-D * WS-D > WS-N OR WS-PRIME = 0
        DIVIDE WS-N BY WS-D GIVING WS-Q REMAINDER WS-R
        IF WS-R = 0 MOVE 0 TO WS-PRIME END-IF
    END-PERFORM.
